\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces The XRD spectra for (a) (HfO$_{2}$)$_{1-x}$(SiO$_{2}$)$_{x}$ and (b) (HfO$_{2}$)$_{1-x}$(GeO$_{2}$)$_{x}$ plotted for several different Hf cation compositions. The observed patterns between Si and Ge doped HfO$_{2}$ are highly similar, demonstrating their chemical resemblance. The diffraction pattern for the mixed films show that the monoclinic phase is the dominant phase, however comparison with available diffraction patterns suggest the presence of other metastable phases. For reference the diffraction pattern of pure HfO$_{2}$ is shown at the bottom. The weak reflections reveal the presence of partially crystalline domains.\relax }}{94}}
