\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.5}{\ignorespaces XRD spectra for (a) (Nb$_{2}$O$_{5}$)$_{1-x}$(GeO$_{2}$)$_{x}$ and (b) (Ta$_{2}$O$_{5}$)$_{1-x}$(SnO$_{2}$)$_{x}$ plotted for several cation compositions. The lack of any discernible diffraction peaks indicate that the (Nb$_{2}$O$_{5}$)$_{1-x}$(GeO$_{2}$)$_{x}$ is x-ray amorphous for the entire composition range probed. (Ta$_{2}$O$_{5}$)$_{1-x}$(SnO$_{2}$)$_{x}$ is x-ray amorphous for high Ta$_{2}$O$_{5}$ rich composition, but crystallizes at high SnO$_{2}$ concentrations.\relax }}{100}}
